WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.492
Step four is grading evidence.

00:00:02.492 --> 00:00:05.617
The example grader is intentionally simple.

00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:12.122
It looks for signals related to returns, days, and delivery, and then produces a score.

00:00:12.122 --> 00:00:17.130
This is useful for teaching because you can see exactly why the score changes.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:25.529
In a real project, you may replace this with a reranker, a classifier, structured L L M output,

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:30.979
or domain-specific rules. The important part is the interface.

00:00:30.979 --> 00:00:36.074
The controller calls grade documents and receives a predictable result.

00:00:36.074 --> 00:00:39.227
The internal implementation can improve later.

00:00:39.907 --> 00:00:46.809
Make evidence quality observable. If a grade fails, you should be able to inspect why.

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:51.173
A mysterious yes or no result makes debugging much harder.
